// Title: Wget Creating Files in Tmp Directory
// Sigma ID: 35a05c60-9012-49b6-a11f-6bab741c9f74
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Joseliyo Sanchez, @Joseliyo_Jstnk
// Date: 2023-06-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Detects the use of wget to download content in a temporary directory such as "/tmp" or
//   "/var/tmp"
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate downloads of files in the tmp folder.
// References:
//   - https://blogs.jpcert.or.jp/en/2023/05/gobrat.html
//   - https://jstnk9.github.io/jstnk9/research/GobRAT-Malware/
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/60bcd645450e4c846238cf0e7226dc40c84c96eba99f6b2cffcd0ab4a391c8b3/detection
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3e44c807a25a56f4068b5b8186eee5002eed6f26d665a8b791c472ad154585d1/detection
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/linux/file_event/file_event_lnx_wget_download_file_in_tmp_dir.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/wget" and (FolderPath startswith "/tmp/" or FolderPath startswith "/var/tmp/")
